      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "carryover_21",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "carryover_percentage",
            value: 40,
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "ai_aggression",
            value: 1.0,
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "ai_caution",
            value: -1.0,
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "carryover_bonus",
            value: "yes",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_22",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "sad.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("After conquering Castle Angthurim, the party set off after Rakshas, hoping that Hidel’s elves had been able to hold him."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_23",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Orcs are heavy-footed creatures; Rakshas’s trail was readily followed. But an ominous silence, broken only by the cawing of ravens, brooded over the road he had taken."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_24",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Soon they encountered the wrack of a great battle. Bodies of elves and orcs lay everywhere. Broken weapons and smashed armor were strewn about and elvish arrows and orcish bolts bristled from the nearby trees. The ground was red with blood."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_25",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("There were some survivors. Father Morvin oversaw their healing, while Tallin followed Eryssa as she anxiously walked among the dead."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_26",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Suddenly, Eryssa cried out. In front of her lay Hidel."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_27",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "heroes_rite.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Scattered around him were the bodies of at least three orcish warlords, and nearly a score of grunts, warriors and crossbowmen. His weapons were notched and broken; his armor dented and smashed. It was clear that his fall had been a battle of valor and glory, worthy to be remembered in the songs of all the kindred races until the end of days."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_28",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("With tears streaming down her face, Eryssa knelt and cradled his head in her lap. As she stroked his face, his eyes fluttered open."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_29",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hidel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ I am sorry, my lady... We held him for... as long as we could... but his bodyguards... were... just too many and powerful... And then... the orcish... reinforcements arrived..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_30",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Her face streaked with tears, Eryssa gazed imploringly at Father Morvin and Sister Thera. They sighed and shook their heads. In a broken voice Eryssa addressed him:"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_31",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Eryssa.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Hidel, I am sorry. I have sent you to your death."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_32",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hidel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ ... Don’t tax yourself... Eryssa... I have died... a warrior’s death... You should be proud..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_33",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hidel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ ... But... there is... one thing... we... could do. We... managed to... recover the gold... Sisal... took it and... retreated south..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_34",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hidel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ I held out as... long as... I could... but they... defeated us... Rakshas went... east and the... rest... went... after... Sisal..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_35",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hidel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Now... uphold the honor... of the Northern... Elves... Recover... the gold... slay this monster... and bring peace... to the... Northlands... Tallin?"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_36",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("At Hidel’s call Tallin approached. He knelt beside, bowing his head in respect."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_37",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ At your service, sir."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_38",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hidel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Eryssa has been... my charge ever... since she was born... I now return... to the earth... from which... I sprang... Please take care... of her."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_39",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ I will."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_40",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hidel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Thank you... Tallin... Now I may rest... in... peace... May you... be victorious..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_41",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Then Hidel closed his eyes and took one last breath."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_42",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "love_theme.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Slowly Tallin approached her. He hesitated before wrapping her gently in his arms."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_43",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Sobbing against Tallin’s chest, Eryssa told him of the many ways Hidel had cherished and warded her and her sister. How he had comforted their childhood hurts; how in later years, he had guided them in the green paths of the forest, and taught them the deep mysteries of elven-kind."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_44",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("The torrent of childhood memories and the depth of her grief left her unable to speak. She and Tallin sat together silently holding each other for some time."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_45",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("As Tallin comforted Eryssa, the surviving elves gathered all of the fallen warriors, and with the humans’ help, laid them to rest. For Hidel, the dwarves raised a monument so that his heroic death would long be remembered. Then, they came before Tallin and Eryssa."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_46",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Father_Morvin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ My lady... it is a hard thing, I know, but you must put your grief behind you. Or at least, put it aside for a little while. We must go quickly to the aid of Sisal and recover our gold."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_47",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Arthian.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Forge your sorrow into rage, girl, and visit it on the slayers of your kinsmen. Teach them what happens to those who make an enemy of an elf."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_48",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "vengeful.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("At these words, Eryssa arose and wiped away her tears. She took command of the surviving elvish forces, for all knew she was a princess of high rank and looked to Hidel’s ward as their leader. Scarcely a face among them was less grim than her own as they took arms and started down Rakshas’s trail."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_49",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Moments later a gryphon swooped down from overhead and reported battle in a forest just a few leagues south of their position. The remainder of the elvish forces had been espied fighting a desperate battle with the orcs."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_50",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("It seemed to the gryphon that the elves were sore beset. The party quickly turned south and plunged into the forest."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_51",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:make_loyal",
            units: "Tallin,Sisal,Ha_Tuil",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "clock_52",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "turn_limit",
            value: 30,
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "objectives",
        side: 1,
        victory: _("Defeat the orcs"),
        defeat: _("Death of Tallin Death of Ro’Arthian Death of Ro’Sothian Turns run out"),
        children: [
          {
            tag: "defeat",
            condition: "hook",
            hook: "predicate:turn_limit",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_1",
        on: "prestart",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "breaking_the_chains.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "elvish-theme.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "the_king_is_dead.ogg",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_3",
        on: "branch_if_3",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "krash.id",
            equals: "Krash",
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "krash.side",
            value: 4,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:unstore_unit",
            variable: "krash",
            x: "$start_loc.x",
            y: "$start_loc.y",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_2",
        on: "prestart",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:set_variable_dynamic",
            variable: "path_get_the_gold",
